Complete command tree:
  warden agent                         Create, inspect, communicate with, and manage agents
  warden agent list                    List all active agent sessions
  warden agent start                   Spawn an agent — `start --role <ROLE> "<prompt>"` (auto-typed), `start --role <ROLE> --dir <path>` (interactive: open Claude & wait), or `start --role <ROLE> TICKET --type <TYPE>` (managed worktree)
  warden agent status                  Show full status for one session
  warden agent digest                  Summarize what an agent accomplished (files, branch, turns, narrative)
  warden agent fork                    Fork an agent's session into a new managed agent (branches the conversation; the source keeps running)
  warden agent restore                 Recreate and resume a lost/orphaned agent (claude --resume)
  warden agent recover                 Revive archived agent records whose tmux session is still alive (dry run unless --apply)
  warden agent adopt                   Register the Claude session in this directory (resume it under tmux, or register the current tmux session live)
  warden agent attach                  Attach to the agent's tmux session
  warden agent stop                    Tear down an agent — the single umbrella verb (default: terminate + clear record + remove worktree)
  warden agent terminate               Stop an agent: kill its tmux+claude session (keeps the record and worktree) — alias for `stop --keep-record --keep-worktree`
  warden agent done                    Terminate an agent and clear its record (does NOT remove the worktree) — alias for `stop --keep-worktree`
  warden agent delete                  Clear an agent's stored record (archives by default; --hard to purge) — alias for `stop --keep-worktree` (record only)
  warden agent remove-worktree         Remove an agent's git worktree + branch (always asks; --force overrides guards) — alias for `stop --keep-record` (worktree only)
  warden agent send                    Type a message into an agent's claude session and press Enter
  warden agent tail                    Print the recent output of an agent's claude session
  warden agent handoff                 Hand off work: delegate to a new/existing agent (--to), or retire self into a successor (--retire)
  warden agent rotate                  Retire this agent and hand its work to a fresh successor in the same workspace (alias for `handoff --retire`)
  warden agent switch                  Hot-swap an agent session to a different backend, model, or tier mid-task
  warden agent permission-mode         Manage an agent's permission mode
  warden agent permission-mode set     Set the permission mode for an agent
  warden agent role                    Inspect warden's built-in agent roles and tier mappings
  warden agent role list               List the built-in agent roles and their descriptions
  warden agent role set                Switch an agent's built-in role (relaunches to re-inject the persona)
  warden agent role set-tier           Set the default model tier for an agent role (tier-1|tier-2|tier-3)
  warden agent role tier               Inspect and manage role-to-tier mappings
  warden agent role tier list          List agent roles and their default model tiers
  warden agent compact                 Manage an agent's force-compact override
  warden agent compact set             Override force-compact for one agent (interrupt → /compact → resume)
  warden pipeline                      Define and run DAG pipelines of agent jobs
  warden pipeline validate             Validate a pipeline YAML spec without creating it
  warden pipeline create               Create a pipeline from a YAML spec or a built-in template
  warden pipeline template             Built-in pipeline templates
  warden pipeline template list        List the built-in pipeline templates and their placeholders
  warden pipeline list                 List pipelines
  warden pipeline show                 Show a pipeline's jobs and their status
  warden pipeline start                Start a pipeline (spawns jobs with no dependencies)
  warden pipeline pause                Pause a running pipeline (in-flight jobs finish; no new jobs spawn)
  warden pipeline resume               Resume a paused pipeline (spawns jobs that became ready while paused)
  warden pipeline cancel               Cancel a pipeline (terminates running jobs)
  warden pipeline delete               Delete a pipeline's record (must not have live jobs — cancel first)
  warden pipeline emit                 Publish this job's handoff (run from inside a pipeline job)
  warden pipeline edit-job             Edit a pending job's prompt and/or handoff
  warden pipeline retry                Re-run a failed or needs-attention job (reopens skipped descendants)
  warden autopilot                     Turn autopilot mode on/off per repo and show its status
  warden autopilot enable              Enable autopilot for this repo (runs the enable-time preflight)
  warden autopilot disable             Disable autopilot for this repo (kill switch — stops spawning/landing)
  warden autopilot status              Show autopilot status (which repos are enabled, and each run)
  warden autopilot init                Scaffold autopilot adoption in the current repo
  warden autopilot register            Register a named autopilot plan
  warden autopilot land                Land an autopilot worker branch into the integration branch
  warden autopilot run                 Manage registered autopilot runs
  warden autopilot run list            List all registered autopilot runs
  warden autopilot run start           start one autopilot run
  warden autopilot run pause           pause one autopilot run
  warden autopilot run resume          resume one autopilot run
  warden autopilot run stop            stop one autopilot run
  warden autopilot run unregister      unregister one autopilot run
  warden schedule                      Schedule recurring (--cron) or single-shot (--at) agents and pipelines
  warden schedule create               Create a schedule that fires an agent or a pipeline
  warden schedule list                 List schedules
  warden schedule show                 Show one schedule, including its last-run outcome
  warden schedule enable               Enable a schedule so it fires again (re-arms next run)
  warden schedule disable              Disable a schedule so it stops firing (history preserved)
  warden schedule delete               Delete a schedule
  warden project                       Manage repo-local warden configuration: memory, presets, templates, and plugins
  warden project memory                Show or edit this repo's warden project memory (.warden/memory.md)
  warden project preset                Save and list named spawn configs (replay with `warden start --preset <name>`)
  warden project preset list           List saved presets and their defaults
  warden project preset save           Save the given spawn flags as a named preset
  warden project prompt-template       Save and list reusable, variabled prompt templates (fill with `warden start --prompt-template <name> --set VAR=value`)
  warden project prompt-template list  List saved prompt templates and their variables
  warden project prompt-template save  Save a named prompt template with {{VAR}} placeholders
  warden project library               Browse saved spawn presets, prompt templates, and pipeline templates in one place
  warden project library list          List saved spawn presets and built-in pipeline templates
  warden project plugin                Inspect warden's plugin system (#47): custom task types + lifecycle hooks
  warden project plugin list           List registered plugins, their custom task types, and subscribed hook events
  warden workspace                     Inspect and manage warden git worktrees, snapshots, branches, and file collisions
  warden workspace list                List warden worktrees under .worktrees, joined to active/archived records
  warden workspace prune               Reclaim orphaned warden worktrees under .worktrees (always asks; --force overrides guards)
  warden workspace snapshot            Checkpoint an agent's worktree + transcript, list checkpoints, and restore one
  warden workspace snapshot create     Capture the worktree state + transcript of an agent (defaults to the current one)
  warden workspace snapshot list       List snapshots for an agent (newest first); --all for every session
  warden workspace snapshot restore    Re-apply a snapshot onto its recorded worktree (refuses a dirty tree unless --force)
  warden workspace branches            Per-agent CI + branch-vs-main status
  warden workspace conflicts           List files currently being edited by more than one agent
  warden workspace who-is-editing      Show which agents are editing a specific file
  warden git                           Commit, push, sync, and review an agent worktree on warden rails
  warden git commit                    Stage and commit the worktree (warden rails + hooks + bookkeeping)
  warden git push                      Push the current branch to origin (warden rails + bookkeeping)
  warden git sync                      Fetch and rebase the current branch onto its base (warden conflict detect)
  warden git review                    Run the agent backend's native diff review on the worktree
  warden check                         Run project checks and install hook guards
  warden check run                     Run the project's configured checks and report only failures
  warden context                       Read and write the shared context (a namespaced key/value store agents share)
  warden context set                   Set a context key (value inline, or --file / --stdin)
  warden context cas                   Set a key only if its current value matches --expected (atomic compare-and-set)
  warden context append                Atomically append to a key's value (creates it if absent)
  warden context get                   Print the value at a context key
  warden context list                  List context keys (optionally filtered by prefix)
  warden context delete                Delete a context key
  warden message                       Send and receive directed messages between agents
  warden message send                  Send a message to an agent (wakes it if it's idle/waiting)
  warden message inbox                 Show this agent's messages (marks them read)
  warden message wait                  Block until a message arrives (or timeout), then print it
  warden approval                      Manage tool-permission prompts and auto-approve policy
  warden approval list                 List pending tool-permission prompts waiting for an answer
  warden approval answer               Answer a pending tool-permission prompt by option number
  warden approval auto                 Toggle per-agent auto-approve and manage the rule policy
  warden approval auto set             Toggle per-agent auto-approve participation
  warden approval auto rules           Show the live auto-approve policy (default rules + per-agent overrides)
  warden approval auto allow           Append an allow rule to the auto-approve policy
  warden approval auto deny            Append an deny rule to the auto-approve policy
  warden approval auto clear           Clear auto-approve rules (default, or a per-agent override with --agent)
  warden approval auto enable          Enable the auto-approve policy (global, or per-agent with --agent)
  warden approval auto disable         Disable the auto-approve policy (global, or per-agent with --agent)
  warden inspect                       Search, audit, export, repair, and measure warden's fleet and resources
  warden inspect resources             Show warden's resource footprint (per-agent memory/CPU, system pressure, daemon stats)
  warden inspect search                Full-text search agents by subject, prompt, type, name, branch, or pane text
  warden inspect history               Browse archived (closed) agents, newest first
  warden inspect audit                 Show recent audited actions, newest last
  warden inspect export                Serialize agent session metadata to JSON on stdout
  warden inspect import                Insert agent session metadata from a JSON dump on stdin
  warden inspect repair                Offline, backup-first repair tools
  warden inspect repair sessions       Diagnose or reconstruct the offline session store
  warden backend                       Inspect and manage the agent-backend registry
  warden backend default               Set the default backend (rejects the reserved local row)
  warden backend disable               Disable a backend so it is no longer used
  warden backend enable                Enable a backend so it may be used
  warden backend list                  List detected backends (installed, tier, default, enabled, limited)
  warden backend rescan                Re-detect installed backend CLIs and print the updated table
  warden backend thinking-mode         Set the internal-thinking routing mode (local_only|free_plus_local)
  warden backend tier                  Set a backend's billing tier (free|subscription|pay_per_use|unclassified)
  warden backend model                 Inspect and manage model catalog and live model menus
  warden backend model list            List models in the catalog and their assigned tiers
  warden backend model tier            Set a model's tier classification (tier-1|tier-2|tier-3)
  warden backend suggest               Recommend local models for the REPL, sized to this machine's memory
  warden backend repl                  Interactive REPL for agents, pipelines, and the git/check lifecycle (local LLM + `/` commands).
  warden usage                         Show provider usage for subscription backends
  warden usage spend                   Show measured Claude spend in dollars, per agent / repo / day
  warden usage savings                 Show the token reductions warden's lifecycle features have earned
  warden usage insights                Mine agent history for patterns and parallelization suggestions
  warden config                        Show the resolved configuration (and its file path)
  warden config path                   Print the resolved config file path
  warden config init                   Create the config file (or migrate it, adding any missing keys and upgrading deprecated flat keys to namespaced blocks)
  warden daemon                        Run the warden hub (HTTP API + poller; the single writer to the file store)
  warden daemon mcp                    Run the MCP stdio server so an orchestrator Claude can manage agents
  warden daemon token                  Manage the daemon's remote-access bearer token
  warden daemon token generate         Generate a random bearer token for remote (non-loopback) access
  warden daemon token show             Print the current bearer token (for pasting into a remote client)
  warden daemon token rotate           Generate a new bearer token, persist it, and restart the daemon
  warden completion                    Generate shell completion scripts
  warden completion bash               Generate bash completion script
  warden completion zsh                Generate zsh completion script
  warden completion fish               Generate fish completion script
  warden completion powershell         Generate PowerShell completion script
  warden setup                         Install missing dependencies (tmux, git, claude; optional gh, ollama)
  warden tutorial                      Run the first-run guided walkthrough of warden's core loop
  warden doctor                        Run preflight checks (required binaries, daemon, data dir, configured local model)
  warden tui                           Live terminal cockpit for agents
  warden version                       Print warden version and build information
  warden start                         Spawn an agent — `start --role <ROLE> "<prompt>"` (auto-typed), `start --role <ROLE> --dir <path>` (interactive: open Claude & wait), or `start --role <ROLE> TICKET --type <TYPE>` (managed worktree)
  warden ls                            List all active agent sessions
  warden status                        Show full status for one session
  warden send                          Type a message into an agent's claude session and press Enter
  warden commit                        Stage and commit the worktree (warden rails + hooks + bookkeeping)
  warden push                          Push the current branch to origin (warden rails + bookkeeping)
  warden sync                          Fetch and rebase the current branch onto its base (warden conflict detect)

